                    "class": "section-number selfRef",
                    "href": "#section-2",
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "textContent": "2. ",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "nodeName": "a",
                  "type": "Element",
                },
                {
                  "attributes": {
                    "class": "section-name selfRef",
                    "href": "#name-streams",
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "textContent": "Streams",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "nodeName": "a",
                  "type": "Element",
                },
                {
                  "textContent": "
      ",
                  "type": "Text",
                },
              ],
              "nodeName": "h2",
              "type": "Element",
            },
            {
              "textContent": "
",
              "type": "Text",
            },
            {
              "attributes": {
                "id": "section-2-1",
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "textContent": "Streams in QUIC provide a lightweight, ordered byte-stream abstraction to an
application. Streams can be unidirectional or bidirectional.",
                  "type": "Text",
                },
                {
                  "attributes": {
                    "class": "pilcrow",
                    "href": "#section-2-1",
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "textContent": "¶",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "nodeName": "a",
                  "type": "Element",
                },
              ],
              "nodeName": "p",
              "type": "Element",
            },
            {
              "textContent": "
",
              "type": "Text",
            },
            {
              "attributes": {
                "id": "section-2-2",
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "textContent": "Streams can be created by sending data. Other processes associated with stream
management -- ending, canceling, and managing flow control -- are all designed
to impose minimal overheads. For instance, a single STREAM frame
(",
                  "type": "Text",
                },
                {
                  "attributes": {
                    "class": "xref",
                    "href": "#frame-stream",
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "textContent": "Section 19.8",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "nodeName": "a",
                  "type": "Element",
                },
                {
                  "textContent": ") can open, carry data for, and close a stream. Streams can
also be long-lived and can last the entire duration of a connection.",
                  "type": "Text",
                },
                {
                  "attributes": {
                    "class": "pilcrow",
                    "href": "#section-2-2",
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "textContent": "¶",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "nodeName": "a",
                  "type": "Element",
                },
              ],
              "nodeName": "p",
              "type": "Element",
            },
            {
              "textContent": "
",
              "type": "Text",
            },
            {
              "attributes": {
                "id": "section-2-3",
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "textContent": "Streams can be created by either endpoint, can concurrently send data
interleaved with other streams, and can be canceled. QUIC does not provide any
means of ensuring ordering between bytes on different streams.",
                  "type": "Text",
                },
                {
                  "attributes": {
                    "class": "pilcrow",
                    "href": "#section-2-3",
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "textContent": "¶",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "nodeName": "a",
                  "type": "Element",
                },
              ],
              "nodeName": "p",
              "type": "Element",
            },
            {
              "textContent": "
",
              "type": "Text",
            },
            {
              "attributes": {
                "id": "section-2-4",
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "textContent": "QUIC allows for an arbitrary number of streams to operate concurrently and for
an arbitrary amount of data to be sent on any stream, subject to flow control
constraints and stream limits; see ",
                  "type": "Text",
                },
                {
                  "attributes": {
                    "class": "xref",
                    "href": "#flow-control",
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "textContent": "Section 4",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "nodeName": "a",
                  "type": "Element",
                },
                {
                  "textContent": ".",
                  "type": "Text",
                },
                {
                  "attributes": {
                    "class": "pilcrow",
                    "href": "#section-2-4",
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "textContent": "¶",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "nodeName": "a",
                  "type": "Element",
                },
              ],
              "nodeName": "p",
              "type": "Element",
            },
            {
              "textContent": "
",
              "type": "Text",
            },
            {
              "attributes": {
                "id": "stream-id",
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "textContent": "
",
                  "type": "Text",
                },
                {
                  "attributes": {
                    "id": "section-2.1",
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "textContent": "
        ",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                    {
                      "attributes": {
                        "id": "name-stream-types-and-identifier",
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "textContent": "
",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "section-number selfRef",
                            "href": "#section-2.1",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "2.1. ",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "section-name selfRef",
                            "href": "#name-stream-types-and-identifier",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "Stream Types and Identifiers",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": "
        ",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                      ],
                      "nodeName": "h3",
                      "type": "Element",
                    },
                    {
                      "textContent": "
",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                    {
                      "attributes": {
                        "id": "section-2.1-1",
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "textContent": "Streams can be unidirectional or bidirectional.  Unidirectional streams carry
data in one direction: from the initiator of the stream to its peer.
Bidirectional streams allow for data to be sent in both directions.",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "pilcrow",
                            "href": "#section-2.1-1",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "¶",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                      ],
                      "nodeName": "p",
                      "type": "Element",
                    },
                    {
                      "textContent": "
",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                    {
                      "attributes": {
                        "id": "section-2.1-2",
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "textContent": "Streams are identified within a connection by a numeric value, referred to as
the stream ID.  A stream ID is a 62-bit integer (0 to 2",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {},
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "62",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "sup",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": "-1) that is
unique for all streams on a connection.  Stream IDs are encoded as
variable-length integers; see ",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "xref",
                            "href": "#integer-encoding",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "Section 16",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": ".  A QUIC endpoint ",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "bcp14",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "MUST NOT",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "span",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": "
reuse a stream ID within a connection.",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "pilcrow",
                            "href": "#section-2.1-2",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "¶",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                      ],
                      "nodeName": "p",
                      "type": "Element",
                    },
                    {
                      "textContent": "
",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                    {
                      "attributes": {
                        "id": "section-2.1-3",
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "textContent": "The least significant bit (0x01) of the stream ID identifies the initiator of
the stream.  Client",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {},
                          "children": [],
                          "nodeName": "wbr",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": "-initiated",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {},
                          "children": [],
                          "nodeName": "wbr",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": " streams have even-numbered stream IDs (with the
bit set to 0), and server",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {},
                          "children": [],
                          "nodeName": "wbr",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": "-initiated",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {},
                          "children": [],
                          "nodeName": "wbr",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": " streams have odd-numbered stream IDs (with
the bit set to 1).",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "pilcrow",
                            "href": "#section-2.1-3",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "¶",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                      ],
                      "nodeName": "p",
                      "type": "Element",
                    },
                    {
                      "textContent": "
",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                    {
                      "attributes": {
                        "id": "section-2.1-4",
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "textContent": "The second least significant bit (0x02) of the stream ID distinguishes between
bidirectional streams (with the bit set to 0) and unidirectional streams (with
the bit set to 1).",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "pilcrow",
                            "href": "#section-2.1-4",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "¶",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                      ],
                      "nodeName": "p",
                      "type": "Element",
                    },
                    {
                      "textContent": "
",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                    {
                      "attributes": {
                        "id": "section-2.1-5",
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "textContent": "The two least significant bits from a stream ID therefore identify a stream as
one of four types, as summarized in ",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "xref",
                            "href": "#stream-id-types",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "Table 1",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": ".",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "pilcrow",
                            "href": "#section-2.1-5",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "¶",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                      ],
                      "nodeName": "p",
                      "type": "Element",
                    },
                    {
                      "textContent": "
",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                    {
                      "attributes": {
                        "id": "name-stream-id-types",
                      },
                      "children": [],
