",
              "type": "Text",
            },
            {
              "attributes": {
                "id": "section-7-4",
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "textContent": "The CRYPTO frame can be sent in different packet number spaces
(",
                  "type": "Text",
                },
                {
                  "attributes": {
                    "class": "xref",
                    "href": "#packet-numbers",
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "textContent": "Section 12.3",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "nodeName": "a",
                  "type": "Element",
                },
                {
                  "textContent": ").  The offsets used by CRYPTO frames to ensure ordered
delivery of cryptographic handshake data start from zero in each packet number
space.",
                  "type": "Text",
                },
                {
                  "attributes": {
                    "class": "pilcrow",
                    "href": "#section-7-4",
                  },
                  "children": [
