            },
            {
              "attributes": {
                "id": "section-7-7",
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "textContent": "Endpoints can use packets sent during the handshake to test for Explicit
Congestion Notification (ECN) support; see ",
                  "type": "Text",
                },
                {
                  "attributes": {
                    "class": "xref",
                    "href": "#ecn",
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "textContent": "Section 13.4",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                  ],
                  "nodeName": "a",
                  "type": "Element",
                },
                {
                  "textContent": ". An endpoint validates
support for ECN by observing whether the ACK frames acknowledging the first
packets it sends carry ECN counts, as described in ",
                  "type": "Text",
                },
                {
                  "attributes": {
                    "class": "xref",
                    "href": "#ecn-validation",
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "textContent": "Section 13.4.2",
