                    {
                      "textContent": "
",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                    {
                      "attributes": {
                        "id": "section-7.1-1",
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "textContent": "Details of how TLS is integrated with QUIC are provided in ",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {},
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "[",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                            {
                              "attributes": {
                                "class": "xref",
                                "href": "#QUIC-TLS",
                              },
                              "children": [
                                {
                                  "textContent": "QUIC-TLS",
                                  "type": "Text",
                                },
                              ],
                              "nodeName": "a",
                              "type": "Element",
                            },
                            {
                              "textContent": "]",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "span",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": ", but
some examples are provided here.  An extension of this exchange to support
client address validation is shown in ",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "xref",
                            "href": "#validate-retry",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "Section 8.1.2",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": ".",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "pilcrow",
                            "href": "#section-7.1-1",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "¶",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                      ],
                      "nodeName": "p",
                      "type": "Element",
                    },
                    {
                      "textContent": "
",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                    {
                      "attributes": {
                        "id": "section-7.1-2",
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "textContent": "Once any address validation exchanges are complete, the
cryptographic handshake is used to agree on cryptographic keys.  The
cryptographic handshake is carried in Initial (",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "xref",
                            "href": "#packet-initial",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "Section 17.2.2",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": ") and Handshake
(",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "xref",
                            "href": "#packet-handshake",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "Section 17.2.4",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": ") packets.",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "pilcrow",
                            "href": "#section-7.1-2",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "¶",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                      ],
                      "nodeName": "p",
                      "type": "Element",
                    },
                    {
                      "textContent": "
",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                    {
                      "attributes": {
                        "id": "section-7.1-3",
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "xref",
                            "href": "#tls-1rtt-handshake",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "Figure 5",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": " provides an overview of the 1-RTT handshake.  Each line
shows a QUIC packet with the packet type and packet number shown first, followed
by the frames that are typically contained in those packets. For instance, the
first packet is of type Initial, with packet number 0, and contains a CRYPTO
frame carrying the ClientHello.",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "pilcrow",
                            "href": "#section-7.1-3",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "¶",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                      ],
                      "nodeName": "p",
                      "type": "Element",
                    },
                    {
                      "textContent": "
",
                      "type": "Text",
                    },
                    {
                      "attributes": {
                        "id": "section-7.1-4",
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "textContent": "Multiple QUIC packets -- even of different packet types -- can be coalesced into
a single UDP datagram; see ",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "xref",
                            "href": "#packet-coalesce",
                          },
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "textContent": "Section 12.2",
                              "type": "Text",
                            },
                          ],
                          "nodeName": "a",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": ". As a result, this handshake
could consist of as few as four UDP datagrams, or any number more (subject to
limits inherent to the protocol, such as congestion control and
anti",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {},
                          "children": [],
                          "nodeName": "wbr",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": "-amplification",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {},
                          "children": [],
                          "nodeName": "wbr",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": ").",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {},
                          "children": [],
                          "nodeName": "wbr",
                          "type": "Element",
                        },
                        {
                          "textContent": "  For instance, the server's first flight contains Initial
packets, Handshake packets, and "0.5-RTT data" in 1-RTT packets.",
                          "type": "Text",
                        },
                        {
                          "attributes": {
                            "class": "pilcrow",
                            "href": "#section-7.1-4",
                          },
                          "children": [
